team\nFixed an issue on the SteamVR version of the game that caused players to be unable to close the quick menu in multiplayer 1v1 once they opened it\nFixed AI batters running in place with a bat in their hand in solo 1v1 when they return to home plate after a foul\nFixed players being able to walk out of the booth on the Sandlot field and Koshien Stadium if they\u2019re tall enough\nFixed the full tutorial getting into a stuck state if the player grabs the ball off the field during the end of the batting portion\nFixed an issue causing venues in the multiplayer venue selection menu to go partially off screen and look cut off\nFixed an issue causing teams on the singleplayer opponent selection menu to show up with a lock icon and a green 0 if those teams hadn\u2019t been unlocked\nFixed players no longer being able to throw the microphone out of the booth on Koshien Stadium and Sandlot Field\nFixed the singleplayer venue selection menu having a gap between Koshien Stadium and the Coming Soon Stadium if the player doesn\u2019t own the Twilight Field\nFixed players sometimes being unable to load their customizer on the Quest version of the game despite having an internet connection\nFixed players sometimes seeing their fields locked on the multiplayer venue selection menu when coming back to the locker room after a multiplayer game\nFixed an issue causing players to be able to round bases on a walk in multiplayer 1v1 instead of being auto locked to their next base when it\u2019s reached\nFixed the full tutorial not showing the pick your throwing type or ending congratulations tutorial cards\nFixed the customizer failing to load on the SteamVR version of the game after returning to the locker room twice\nFixed an issue causing the AI vs AI game in announcer mode to sometimes get stuck on a side switchover\nFixed an issue causing human catchers in multiplayer to be able to yank batted balls away from the batter\nFixed an issue in multiplayer 1v1 that completely messes up position selection when a player picks a static fielding position, leaves the game, then rejoins the same game\nFixed an issue in multiplayer 1v1 that occasionally causes players to end up on the same side (both fielders or both batters) after an inning changeover\nImprovements:\nMade the ball stop sitting on the ground while the catcher waits to throw it back to the pitcher in multiplayer 1v1\nMade AI fielders more reactive on fumbles in multiplayer 1v1", "created_date": 1781731219, "id": "27263413923277578", "version": "2.5880", "version_code": 5880, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": {"id": "27263408116611492"}, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}, {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "3256881337690839", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "27263413923277578"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": []}, "change_log": null, "created_date": 1781215931, "id": "27189040684048236", "version": "2.5879", "version_code": 5879, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": {"id": "27189036284048676"}, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}, {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "3256881337690839", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "27263413923277578"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": [{"channel_name": "LIVE", "id": "3208127792574896"}]}, "change_log": "Patch Notes (Live v2.5878):\nBug Fixes:\nResolved an issue causing the Zevo Games introductory splash screen to cut itself short on the SteamVR and Viveport versions of the game.\nClicking the join button on a game within the lobby browser no longer results in an infinite hung loading screen when the join process silently fails. Instead, the player now correctly gets returned to the lobby browser.\nThe current play now properly resets when dropping the ball at the AI pitcher\u2019s feet in 1v1\nHuman catchers can no longer yank the ball away from the human batter in 1v1, robbing the batter from batting the ball\nFixed AI runners in 1v1 running bases when the ball is dropped in the outfield after a walk or an overthrow\nFixed the game treating walks as in play balls when the human batter is beaned but hits the ball with the bat at the same time\nFixed the AI catcher getting sometimes stuck on walk events and not throwing the ball back to the pitcher\nFixed AI runners running 2 bases on an overthrow if the ball is dropped in the outfield right before they reach base\nFixed AI runners sometimes stealing home from third base on a foul ball\nFixed players sometimes not being able to grab the skip lever\nFixed players sometimes not being able to manually grab the ball\nFixed the player slowly sinking into the ground over time\nFixed an issue preventing players from creating another multiplayer game after going into a multiplayer game and backing out to the lobby together\nApplied a general fix for the AI catcher sometimes getting stuck in multiplayer 1v1\nFixed an issue causing paid players to see the cannon, special pitches, and batflips purchase prompts\nFixed an issue causing the joined player in multiplayer 1v1 to either end up on a black screen or see their TV menu turn off when the host appears in the locker room for them if they got to the locker room before the host did\nFixed the 1v1 and free roam menu titles showing up at the same time when a created lobby is still loading\nFixed players being taggable on a homerun in multiplayer 1v1 if the ball bounces off the fence before leaving the field\nImprovements:\nAdjusted the shader on the local player\u2019s hands to match the skin shader used on all other bodies in the game\nMade AI players in multiplayer 1v1 attempt to pick up the ball again after fumbling instead of just standing there\nMade the AI catcher in multiplayer 1v1 wait until the foul popup finishes playing to throw the ball back to the pitcher", "created_date": 1780439040, "id": "27075209725431333", "version": "2.5878", "version_code": 5878, "release_status": "RELEASED", "status": "APPROVED", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": {"id": "27075205745431731"}, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}, {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "__isAppBinary": "AndroidBinary", "binary_application": {"__typename": "Application", "id": "3256881337690839", "is_concept": false, "latest_released_binary": {"__typename": "AndroidBinary", "id": "27263413923277578"}, "release_status": "RELEASED"}, "binary_release_channels": {"nodes": []}, "change_log": null, "created_date": 1780093163, "id": "27019762814309358", "version": "2.5877", "version_code": 5877, "release_status": "PENDING", "status": "DRAFT", "binary_test_results": {"nodes": []}, "obb_binary": {"id": "27019758374309802"}, "asset_files": {"count": 0}, "debug_symbols": {"count": 0}, "__isAppBinaryWithFileAsset": "AndroidBinary"}]}}, "viewer": {"user": null}}}